  "habitat": "Mixed bushveld, woodland, riverine forest and forest edges, and degraded areas with trees. Often in large gardens and parks. Usually hunts insects from a low branch away from water, and occasionally fishes.",
  "summary": "A common dry-land kingfisher with a streaked brown head, a heavy red bill, a blue rump and tail, and a buffy streaked breast and flanks. Males have a black mantle and shoulders; females are brown there and, in Wikipedia, more streaked below. In flight the underwings are cinnamon. Wikipedia is the only source used here for carmine legs (recorded as red), a dark brown iris, and a brown bill tip; Newman's calls the bill wholly red.",
  "sampleData": false,
  "similar": [
    {
      "slug": "halcyon-leucocephala",
      "note": "Grey-headed has a plain grey head and breast, a chestnut belly, and white-and-rufous (not all-cinnamon) underwings. Brown-hooded is larger, with a streaked brown head and streaked buffy breast and flanks (Newman's; eBird)."
    },
    {
      "slug": "halcyon-chelicuti",
      "note": "Striped is smaller and has a two-coloured bill (dark above, red below), a bold black eye-stripe to the nape and a white collar. Brown-hooded's bill is larger, heavier and wholly red (Newman's)."
    },
    {
      "slug": "halcyon-senegalensis",
      "note": "Woodland has a bicoloured bill (red above, black below), a bright turquoise-blue back, and white underparts and head (Newman's; eBird)."
    }
  ],
